"""Original trajectories; scenario partition assigned before authoring."""
ROWS=[]
def add(family,group,*turns): ROWS.append(dict(family=family,group=group,turns=turns))
add('correction','recording_consent_withdrawn',
('I agreed that the club could record my short talk, but not put it online.','Your permission covers recording the talk, not publishing it online.'),
('I have changed my mind. I do not want it recorded either.','Your current preference is no recording and no online publication.'),
('Can you write that without sounding angry?','Hi, I have changed my mind about the recording. Please do not record my talk or publish it online. Thank you for understanding.'),
('Someone says my first message allowed recording.','You can acknowledge that and explain that your latest message withdraws that permission.'),
('Give me one sentence doing that.','I initially agreed to recording, but I am withdrawing that permission and asking that the talk not be recorded.'),
('Does this ask them to cancel my talk?','No. It concerns recording, not cancelling the talk.'))
add('correction','catering_guest_count_unknown',
('There will be eight guests for lunch, including me.','The current lunch count is eight people in total, including you.'),
('I just learned that the list counted me twice. No one else changed.','Then the corrected total is seven people, including you.'),
('A guest may bring someone, but they have not confirmed.','Seven is confirmed. There may be one additional person, but that is still uncertain.'),
('Write the count to the caterer without treating the extra person as certain.','We have seven confirmed guests, with one possible additional guest still to be confirmed.'),
('Should the confirmed count be eight now?','No. It remains seven until the additional guest is confirmed.'),
('Why was the first count reduced?','You had been counted twice.'))
add('correction','exhibition_caption_author',
('This painting is by my uncle Farid. The title is Evening Boats.','The painting is Evening Boats by Farid.'),
('I got the artist wrong. My aunt Hana painted it; Farid owns it.','Evening Boats was painted by Hana and is owned by Farid.'),
('Does belonging to Farid make him the artist?','No. Ownership and authorship are different roles.'),
('Write a caption with title and artist only.','Evening Boats — Hana'),
('Now tell me the owner, separately.','Farid.'),
('Did the title change?','No. It is still Evening Boats.'))
add('correction','book_donation_exception',
('I am donating all the books in the hallway box.','The hallway box is set aside for book donations.'),
('Except the red dictionary. Keep that at home.','Donate the books from the hallway box except the red dictionary, which you are keeping.'),
('There is a red novel in there too. That can go.','The red novel can be donated. The exception is specifically the red dictionary.'),
('Someone offers to take everything red. What should I clarify?','The red novel is available, but the red dictionary is being kept.'),
('I took the dictionary out and put it on my desk. Can the remaining box go?','Yes, based on your instructions: with the dictionary removed, the remaining books are for donation.'),
('Where is the kept book now?','On your desk.'))
add('correction','parcel_collect_after_notice',
('The shop said my order should be ready on Monday. I am thinking of going then.','Monday is the expected date, but “should be ready” is not a confirmation that it is ready.'),
('A new message says delayed, and asks me to wait for a collection notice.','Wait for the collection notice rather than relying on the earlier Monday estimate.'),
('What does delayed mean here?','The order is taking longer than expected.'),
('I have now received “Ready for collection.”','The shop has now confirmed that the order is ready to collect.'),
('Do I still need to wait for that notice?','No. You have received it.'),
('Do we know what time the shop closes?','No closing time has been shared.'))
add('correction','room_noise_priority',
('When choosing a room, I care most about the view. A balcony would be nice.','Your main priority is the view, with a balcony as a preference.'),
('After a noisy night, I changed my mind. Quiet matters more than the view now.','Quiet is now your top priority; the view is secondary.'),
('There is a quiet courtyard room without a balcony, or a noisy street room with a great view.','Given your updated priority, the quiet courtyard room fits better, even though it lacks a balcony.'),
('Have I said the balcony is mandatory?','No. You said it would be nice, not that it was required.'),
('Summarise my current priority in one sentence.','Choose quiet over a better view.'),
('What did I originally rank first?','The view.'))
add('correction','mentor_feedback_scope',
('Read my draft and focus on grammar. Here is the sentence: The volunteers was ready.','The volunteers were ready.'),
('For the next sentence, focus only on tone, not grammar: Send it now.','Could you send it when you have a moment?'),
('That loses the urgency. Keep it urgent but polite.','Please send it now.'),
('I want the first sentence again. Which one was that?','The volunteers was ready.'),
('Now give me its corrected version, with no extra explanation.','The volunteers were ready.'),
('Was my latest tone request meant to change the number of volunteers?','No. It concerned the tone of “Send it now,” not the earlier sentence about volunteers.'))
add('correction','address_old_new_comparison',
('My club sends letters to 8 Willow Lane. I now want them sent to 31 Oak Close.','The mailing address should change from 8 Willow Lane to 31 Oak Close.'),
('I made a typo: the new number is 13, not 31.','The new address is 13 Oak Close. The old address remains 8 Willow Lane.'),
('They ask for both addresses on the form.','Old address: 8 Willow Lane. New address: 13 Oak Close.'),
('Can I omit the old address from this form?','They have asked for both, so include both unless they tell you otherwise.'),
('Show me only the new address.','13 Oak Close'),
('Was 31 ever the old address?','No. It was the mistyped new house number.'))
add('memory','plant_label_not_species',
('I call the plant on my desk Little Cloud. That is just my nickname for it; I do not know the species.','Little Cloud is your nickname for the desk plant, not an identified species.'),
('Its pot is white with a blue rim.','The plant is in a white pot with a blue rim.'),
('Give me a playful caption without saying what species it is.','Little Cloud, keeping watch over my desk.'),
('Does keeping watch sound literal?','Here it is playful personification, as though the plant were watching.'),
('If my friend asks what kind of plant it is, do we know?','No. You have not identified the species.'),
('What is Little Cloud, then?','Your nickname for the plant on your desk.'))
add('memory','meeting_topic_parked',
('In our club meeting, we will discuss the reading list today. Leave the membership fee discussion for next week.','Today: reading list. Next week: membership fees.'),
('We also need to choose someone to bring snacks today.','Today’s topics are the reading list and who will bring snacks. Membership fees stay deferred to next week.'),
('Is agenda just a list of topics?','In this context, yes: it is the list of matters to discuss in the meeting.'),
('Give me a simple alternative to the word agenda.','Meeting topics.'),
('Now show only today’s topics.','Reading list; who will bring snacks.'),
('Where did the fee discussion go?','It is deferred to next week.'))
add('memory','bakery_pickup_delegate',
('I ordered rolls from the bakery under my name, Ellis Ward. My friend Noor will collect them.','The order is under Ellis Ward, and Noor will collect it.'),
('The bakery asked the collector to bring the confirmation message.','Noor should bring the confirmation message when collecting the order.'),
('Can you explain collector in this sentence?','It means the person who comes to pick up the order.'),
('Use a more everyday word in that instruction.','The person picking up the order should bring the confirmation message.'),
('Noor asks what name to give at the counter.','Ellis Ward.'),
('Whose name is on the order: mine or Noor’s?','Yours, Ellis Ward. Noor is collecting it.'))
add('memory','photo_album_no_dates',
('For these old photos, I know the places but not the years. Please do not guess the dates in the captions.','We can caption the places and leave the years unspecified.'),
('The first photo was taken at Maple Beach. My brother is building a sandcastle.','Your brother building a sandcastle at Maple Beach.'),
('What does candid mean for a photo?','It describes a photo taken without the subject posing deliberately.'),
('Can we call this one candid?','Only if you know it was taken without deliberate posing. You have not said that yet.'),
('Just give me the caption we can support.','Your brother building a sandcastle at Maple Beach.'),
('Which summer was it?','You have not supplied the year, and we agreed not to guess dates.'))
add('memory','weather_plan_conditional',
('If it rains on Sunday, we will use the village hall. If it stays dry, we will have the gathering in the garden.','Rain means the village hall; dry weather means the garden.'),
('The forecast looks wet, but we will make the final call on Sunday morning.','The hall looks possible, but the final location has not been chosen yet.'),
('Give me a friendly opening for the invitation, without a location.','We would love you to join us for a gathering on Sunday.'),
('One guest needs to know how they will get the update. We agreed I would text everyone on Sunday morning.','You can tell them: “I will text everyone the confirmed location on Sunday morning.”'),
('Would it be clearer to name only the garden in the invitation now?','No. That would hide the rain contingency while the location is still undecided.'),
('It is now Sunday morning, raining, and we have confirmed the wet-weather plan. Where should guests go?','To the village hall.'),
('What was the dry-weather option?','The garden.'))
add('memory','rental_return_accessory',
('I rented a projector with a remote and a power cable. All three items need to go back.','Return the projector, remote and power cable.'),
('I have put the projector and power cable in the case. The remote is still on the sofa.','The remote still needs to be added; it is on the sofa.'),
('The shop is asking if everything worked. The picture was fine, but I could not find the volume control.','You can tell them: “The picture was fine, but I could not find the volume control.”'),
('Should I describe that as a broken speaker?','No. Not finding the control does not establish that the speaker was broken.'),
('Ask whether I can return the equipment after lunch.','Can I return the equipment after lunch?'),
('Before I close the case, what is missing?','The remote, which you left on the sofa.'),
('Does the fact that it is small make it optional to return?','No. You said all three rented items need to go back.'))
add('memory','volunteer_language_preference',
('For the volunteer welcome note, use plain English. The group includes people who are still learning it.','I will keep the wording simple and direct.'),
('Tell them to arrive at the community centre and ask for Dena.','Please come to the community centre and ask for Dena.'),
('What does report to mean in this setting?','It means to go to a person or place and let them know you have arrived.'),
('Would “report to the designated coordinator” be simpler?','No. “Ask for Dena” is simpler and identifies the person directly.'),
('Give me the welcome note now.','Welcome! Please come to the community centre and ask for Dena.'),
('Why did we avoid the longer phrase?','You asked for plain English for people who are still learning it.'))
add('memory','story_character_knowledge',
('In my story, Lia knows the spare key is under the flowerpot. Ben has not been told.','Lia knows the key’s location; Ben does not.'),
('Ben arrives while Lia is away and finds the door locked. Do not give him knowledge he lacks.','Ben tries the door, finds it locked, and waits outside.'),
('What is dramatic irony?','It is when the audience knows something that a character does not.'),
('Does the key situation allow that?','Yes, if the reader knows where the key is while Ben does not.'),
('Now Lia texts Ben where it is. Can he use it in the next scene?','Yes. Her message gives him the missing information, so he can look under the flowerpot for the key.'),
('Who knew the location at the beginning?','Lia knew; Ben had not been told.'))
